==English==
{{wikipedia}}
{{was wotd|2012|February|7}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|senescere||to grow [[old]]|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/sɨnˈɛsəns/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{context|biology|lang=en}} The [[state]] or [[process]] of [[ageing]], especially in [[humans]]; old age.
# {{context|cell biology|lang=en}} Ceasing to divide by [[mitosis]] because of shortening of [[telomere]]s or excessive [[DNA]] damage.
# {{context|gerontology|lang=en}} Old age; accumulated damage to [[macromolecule]]s, [[cell]]s, [[tissue]]s and [[organ]]s with the passage of time.
# {{context|botany|lang=en}} Fruit senescence, leading to ripening of fruit.

